    findings: ["Overall hazard ratio of death 0.89 (95 percent confidence interval 0.82 to 0.96; P equals 0.005), a five-year absolute benefit of 5.4 percent.", "Benefit varied with stage (test for trend P equals 0.04): stage IA hazard ratio 1.40 (0.95 to 2.06), stage IB 0.93 (0.78 to 1.10), stage II 0.83 (0.73 to 0.95), stage III 0.83 (0.72 to 0.94).", "No significant interaction with the drug given alongside cisplatin: vinorelbine 0.80 (0.70 to 0.91), etoposide or vinca alkaloid 0.92 (0.80 to 1.07), other 0.97 (0.84 to 1.13).", "Chemotherapy effect was higher in patients with better performance status.", "No interaction with sex, age, histology, type of surgery, planned radiotherapy or planned total cisplatin dose.", "No heterogeneity of chemotherapy effect between the five trials."],
