    summary: "The CROWN trial investigators, reported by Shaw, Bauer, de Marinis and colleagues with Solomon as senior author, randomised 296 patients with advanced ALK-positive non-small-cell lung cancer and no previous systemic treatment for metastatic disease between lorlatinib and crizotinib. The primary endpoint was blinded independent central review progression-free survival; intracranial response was a secondary endpoint.\n\nThe cost is a distinctive toxicity profile: hyperlipidaemia and central nervous system effects on mood, speed and memory. Lorlatinib is the first lung cancer drug whose main side effect is cognitive, which makes the choice between it and alectinib a quality-of-life question rather than a purely efficacy one.",
